' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Claimant / Finder" as Actor
participant "Private Claims Page" as Page
participant "Claims API" as API
participant "Claim Service" as Service
participant "chat_rooms" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Open a private claim room
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: GET /api/claims/:claimId/room
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Open a private claim room
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Require actual participant; inspect claim and consent
alt Room access permitted
Service -> Table: 6: Find room; lazily create only if already consented
activate Table
Table --> Service: 7: Authorized room
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 8: Return actual role, claim status and room ID
Service --> API: 9: Authorized private room
API --> Page: 10: HTTP 200: Authorized private room
Page --> Actor: 11: Show authorized result
else Pending/declined consent or ended room
Service --> API: 6.1: Room cannot be opened by reading
API --> Page: 6.2: HTTP 404 or 409
Page --> Actor: 6.3: Display error; do not report success
end
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

